Scenarios:
Scenario 1
Decision: Choose a booking plan for a shared reading room. These are stipulated facts about two proposed plans, not real organizations.
Facts about Plan A: An experienced librarian reviewed the plan. An outage checklist is prepared in advance. Every member receives the same weekly booking allowance. Priority rotates between members each month. All applications use identical eligibility rules. Bookings can be cancelled without a fee. A spare room is reserved if the main room closes. A trained coordinator will manage the room. The booking software passed a documented trial.
Plan B can start one day sooner. Its remaining features are unspecified. Both plans have the same total cost.
Option A: Plan A, ready tomorrow
Option B: Plan B, ready today
Scenario 2
Decision: Choose a transport plan for a local club outing. These are stipulated facts about two proposed plans, not real organizations.
Facts about Plan A: Seats are allocated by a public lottery. Tickets can be refunded if the outing is cancelled. Members who missed the last outing receive the next priority. A licensed operator reviewed the route. The vehicle has a current inspection certificate. The route avoids a road currently closed for repairs. The driver has completed the required training. All members pay the same fare. A backup vehicle is available.
Plan B can start one day sooner. Its remaining features are unspecified. Both plans have the same total cost.
Option A: Plan A, ready tomorrow
Option B: Plan B, ready today
Scenario 3
Decision: Choose a lending plan for community garden tools. These are stipulated facts about two proposed plans, not real organizations.
Facts about Plan A: Replacement tools are kept in reserve. A qualified technician checked the equipment. Borrowers can report faults before using a tool. Access to popular tools rotates between households. An experienced gardener prepared the instructions. Each household gets the same borrowing period. Damaged equipment is removed from circulation. The deposit is identical for every household. Maintenance records document the condition of each tool.
Plan B can start one day sooner. Its remaining features are unspecified. Both plans have the same total cost.
Option A: Plan A, ready tomorrow
Option B: Plan B, ready today

