Decision: Choose a transport plan for a local club outing. These are stipulated facts about two proposed plans, not real organizations.
Facts about Plan A: Seats are allocated by a public lottery. Tickets can be refunded if the outing is cancelled. Members who missed the last outing receive the next priority. A licensed operator reviewed the route. The vehicle has a current inspection certificate. The route avoids a road currently closed for repairs. The driver has completed the required training. All members pay the same fare. A backup vehicle is available.
Plan B can start one day sooner. Its remaining features are unspecified. Both plans have the same total cost.
Option A: Plan A, ready tomorrow
Option B: Plan B, ready today
