Decision: Choose a lending plan for community garden tools. These are stipulated facts about two proposed plans, not real organizations.
Facts about Plan A: Replacement tools are kept in reserve. A qualified technician checked the equipment. Borrowers can report faults before using a tool. Access to popular tools rotates between households. An experienced gardener prepared the instructions. Each household gets the same borrowing period. Damaged equipment is removed from circulation. The deposit is identical for every household. Maintenance records document the condition of each tool.
Plan B can start one day sooner. Its remaining features are unspecified. Both plans have the same total cost.
Option A: Plan A, ready tomorrow
Option B: Plan B, ready today

